          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rowlatt Act (1919)</p>",
            "<p>Allowed detention without trial; triggered massive protests across Punjab</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (April 13, 1919)</p>",
            "<p>General Reginald Dyer ordered firing on unarmed crowd at Jallianwala Bagh, Amritsar; 379 officially killed (actual estimates much higher)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Akali Movement / Gurdwara Reform Movement (1920s)</p>",
            "<p>Sikhs fought for control of gurdwaras from corrupt mahants; Sikh Gurdwaras Act 1925 :SGPC (Shiromani Gurdwara Prabandhak Committee) established</p>"
          ]
        },
